    "body": "Adding a quiz A quiz asks your readers a question, then tells each of them whether they got it right. It's the same element as a poll , with one difference: you mark the correct answer. Making a quiz In the builder, open the Insert bar and choose Poll/Quiz . Click Set up poll or quiz on the new element, or Edit Question & Options in the sidebar. At the top of the Question & Answers tab, choose Quiz . Type your question and fill in the answers. Click Correct? beside the right answer. It changes to ✓ Correct . Optionally, add an Explanation — up to 280 characters, shown to readers after they answer. Click Done . Done won't close a quiz until a correct answer is marked. On a Single choice quiz, one answer is correct. To accept several correct answers, switch Selection to Multiple choice on the Answering tab and mark each one — a reader is right only when they pick exactly those. What readers see Once a reader answers, they see You got it! or Not quite. The answer is … , with the correct answer ticked and your explanation below. Answers are only recorded on the published report — not in the builder or preview. Answering settings On the Answering tab: Changing answers starts at One response only , so a reader can't keep answering until they're right. Show readers chooses what they get back: Right or wrong, and the answer (the default), the same and how everyone answered , or Just a thank-you if you'd rather score it privately. To check the answered state before publishing, select the quiz and click Preview Answer in the sidebar. Nothing is saved. Seeing the results Answers appear in the report's Analytics , on the Polls & Quizzes tab. When a report has both polls and quizzes, each card is labeled Poll or Quiz . A quiz card shows: How many got it right — for example 18 of 24 answered correctly , with a ring showing the percentage. The most common other answer — the answer most readers reached for instead, and how many chose it. It's worth a sentence in your next update. The correct answer, ticked on the bars. Grading happens when you open the tab, so if you change a quiz's correct answer, every response is graded again against the new one. Click Show who responded to see each respondent, their answer, when they answered, and a Result of Correct or Not quite . A reader who opened a personalized link is named; anyone else shows as Anonymous . Search by name or answer, or filter to All , Correct , or Not quite . The list loads 25 at a time. Use the filter as a follow-up list: the readers who answered Not quite are the ones who'll most appreciate hearing the full story. Download CSV exports one row per answer, with the question, the answer, and the respondent's name and constituent ID, plus Correct (Yes or No) and Correct Answer columns. Related Adding a poll Analytics overview"
