    "body": "Creating a collection A collection is a form plus everything it gathers. This guide takes you from an empty Collections view to a form ready to share. Start a new collection In the dashboard, open Collections in the sidebar and click Add new (or click New collection on Home). Storyraise Collect opens in a new tab with a fresh collection. If you're already in Collect, click Start new collection . Then choose what you want to collect, under What do you want to collect? Each option pre-builds a sensible form you can customize: Thank-yous from beneficiaries Stories from program leaders Stories from the field Stories from our community General information I want to upload information — start from existing data via CSV instead of a form Build out your form Your starting form opens in the editor. From here you can add, remove, and reorder fields, and set each field's label, help text, and whether it's required. The full catalog of field types is covered in Form field types . For longer or repeating data, you can split a form into steps — see Multi-step forms . Add people (optional) If you're collecting from people you already know, upload a CSV with an email column into the collection ( Upload a CSV , or Import CSV once it has data). When one of them opens the form through a personalized link (see Sharing your form ), Storyraise finds their row by email and pre-fills what it already knows, and their submission updates that row instead of adding a new one. You can also skip this and simply share the form link with anyone. Empty until responses arrive A new collection shows \"Nothing collected yet. Share your form to start gathering responses, or upload a CSV to begin from existing data.\" — with Open form editor and Upload a CSV to get going. Next Form field types — the building blocks of your form Sharing your form — get it in front of respondents"
